<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror/Mystery</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A series of interstellar radio signals make their way to earth, warning of an impending threat. After the first message, the foundation ensures no other stations can receive the signals.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative (edited):</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">And&nbsp;more</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>Signals are received yearly. Occasionally, a video is sent.</li>
<li>Signals originate from the Canis Major Overdensity, which has been in quarantine for a millennia.</li>
<li>Refer to <strong>Edit</strong></li>
<li>Various abhorrent experiments are performed on the populace to find a way of damaging the mass.</li>
<li>Anomalous chemical in the spinal fluid of 8% of individuals that die in their sleep is discovered to tear apart the mass at the molecular level.</li>
<li>Spinal fluid is dumped on mass. Mass regenerates via absorbing an entire megacity of the home planet.</li>
<li>Mass launches itself into orbit and instantaneously adapts to the conditions. Floating from planet to planet absorbing all life.</li>
<li>Planet the mass is on is encased in a metal alloy. Mass is continually weakened by railgun fire.</li>
<li>Jam causes railgun fire to cease for 20 seconds and mass escapes. Mass tears apart railguns.</li>
<li>Mass emits soundwave, showing it can communicate. &quot;Stop. Leave,&quot; are the only words spoken.</li>
<li>The remaining inhabitants of the galaxy dedicate their existence to keeping the mass from breaching into other galaxies. The inhabitants do this in an attempt to &quot;correct their mistake&quot;.</li>
<li>Mass eventually adapts, emitting a massive heatwave that melts everything exposed to it. It also converted all exposed into the mass itself.</li>
<li>The signals were sent by the last remnants of this civilisation. The final signal reveals the senders to be human.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Edit:</strong> A signal was triggered by an experimental technology that incorporated a sarkic ritual. This resulted in the displacement of the home planet of the signal senders. And a change in the genetic code of 30% of the species. This resulted in the rapid generation of sentient cells that act as a hive mind, think cancer if it had a sense of self. The affected are converted into a fleshy mass.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Throughout the article there are hints that the ones that sent the signals were humans. Additionally, it is progressively revealed that it was an alternate universe foundation that caused earth to be displaced. Having to focus on keeping humanity alive, they didn't notice the genetic change until it was too late.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<p>For a more in-depth look refer to my response to Dyslexion and Petrograd.</p>

