<p>This collapsible will contain an updated and more in-depth version of the concept.</p>
<p><strong>Massive edit:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Lots&nbsp;of&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Sorry&nbsp;for&nbsp;wall&nbsp;of&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The signals reveal that the canis major dwarf galaxy has been in indefinite quarantine for about a millennia. With the alien race having spent this time keeping the mass from breaching containment and exiting the galaxy.</p>
<p>Further information is received a year later, telling of the origin of the mass. At some point, a signal was triggered by an experimental technology which resulted in a change in the genetic code of 30% of the alien race. This change resulted in the rapid generation of sentient cells that act as a hive mind, think cancer if it had a sense of self. The affected individuals quickly became overwhelmed by the cancerous cells, eventually being entirely consumed. The separate smaller masses sought out one another to grow, as they grew in size, they similarly grew in intellect.</p>
<p>Another year passes before another signal is received (this will be a yearly pattern). The sender expresses immense remorse before divulging information relating to damaging the mass, or at least holding it off. The leaders of the alien species performed many experiments, some far less ethical than others. The spinal fluid of approximately 8% of individuals that die in their sleep contains an anomalous chemical that tears apart the mass on the molecular level. However, the aliens are unsure as to whether or not other species have this same chemical.<br />
In an attempt to neutralise the mass, 50 kilolitres of spinal fluid containing the chemical is dropped onto it. The mass essentially begins melting and makes a direct B line to a megacity on the species home planet. Attempts to stop it are unsuccessful and the mass regenerates. After this, it enters orbit by literally launching itself into space. It adapts to the inhospitable conditions near instantaneously, floating from planet to planet, consuming all life it comes across. A total of 50% of the population had been lost due to the increase in aggression of the mass.</p>
<p>A final effort to prevent the mass from ending the civilisation was made, where a planet the mass had just landed at is encased in a metal alloy. The mass is constantly weakened by continuous railgun fire.<br />
Due to a jam that prevented railgun fire for 20 seconds, the mass was able to tear its containment unit to shreds along with the railgun stations. At this point, the mass had grown sufficiently enough to communicate although in a rudimentary way. It emits a soundwave, saying, “Scaring. Leave.”</p>
<p>The alien race dedicates the rest of its existence to reversing what they believe is their mistake, constantly engaging with the mass and preventing it from leaving the galaxy.<br />
Eventually, the mass adapts, emitting a heatwave that spans the entire galaxy. This heatwave has two effects: Burning any living being to death due to its temperature exceeding 1000 degrees Celsius. Secondly, it converts those exposed into separate instances of the mass, which seek out each other and join the main mass.</p>
<p>The last remnants of the alien race; those housed in underground government facilities, are the ones that sent out the signals. The final signal tells of these last remaining aliens, and how they are sorry for the responsibility that has been placed on the surrounding galaxies.<br />
As the mass reaches 5000 lightyears from earth, it sends out its own signals, which contain a LOT of binary. The translated signals are oddly friendly, stating that it will not bring harm and that it is tired.</p>
<p>Communication is established and the foundation conducts a series of interviews by sending out questions in binary and translating the response. The mass talks of its origin, stating that it does not know how it came to be, only that there was darkness then there was light. It was a child, hungry and afraid, but it is older now and understands that eating causes death. It says that it met a being of machine and flesh, which told the mass a “beautiful message”. The mass has refused to eat since it received the message, choosing to observe and learn. Because it has been starving itself, it is dying. It saw earth and its natural wonders and felt that earth would be a nice final destination. The problem is, of course, that the foundation has been given a very gruesome depiction of this mass, and a large mass of flesh that wiped out an entire civilisation is the easiest to trust.</p>
<p>Essentially, an alien civilisation was wiped out by an eldritch abomination that developed due to their use of experimental technology. They sent out a series of messages to explain what happened, and what threat has been unleashed. The foundation is left with a dilemma though. After the mass expresses a desire to not bring harm but rather to have a peaceful death, the foundation is left having to decide what to trust. Additionally, the mass references &quot;others&quot; in the surrounding galaxies, giving a rather grim reason for why we haven't seen much alien life.</p>
<p>I am also considering having the mass speak of a &quot;father&quot;, which will involve some references to Yaldabaoth as a possible reason for the creation of the mass.</p>
